# PROJECT: DeutschSchreiben AI

## 1. Project Overview

Build a full-stack German Writing Assessment and Learning Platform called "DeutschSchreiben AI".

The platform helps learners improve their German writing skills at CEFR levels B1, B2, and C1.

The platform must function as an academic writing assessment system, not simply a grammar correction tool.

The primary goal is to assess original writing, identify linguistic errors, explain mistakes, provide educational feedback, and track long-term learning progress.

## 2. Technology Stack

- Frontend: Next.js, React, TypeScript
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Database: Supabase PostgreSQL
- Authentication: Supabase Auth
- AI: LLM API with structured JSON output
- Hosting: Vercel
- Charts: Recharts

Keep API keys and privileged database operations on the server.

## 3. Language and Target Users

- Website interface: English with Thai feedback support
- Writing language: German only
- Target levels: B1, B2, C1
- Primary users: German language learners
- Feedback language: Thai by default

## 4. Main Pages

Create the following pages:

1. Landing Page
2. Login / Register
3. Dashboard
4. Writing Practice
5. Assessment Results
6. Writing History
7. Learning Center
8. Vocabulary Bank
9. User Profile and Settings

## 5. Writing Task System

Support these writing categories:

- E-Mail
- Brief
- Stellungnahme
- Erörterung
- Bericht
- Beschwerde

Each task must include:

- CEFR level
- Writing category
- Topic
- Instructions
- Requirements
- Minimum and maximum word count
- Suggested time
- Task version

The user completes one writing task per session.

## 6. Writing Editor

Build a clean academic writing editor.

Features:

- German character support
- Automatic word counter
- Character counter
- Paragraph counter
- Autosave drafts
- Undo / Redo
- Submit button
- Submission validation

Do not provide automatic grammar correction while the user is completing an academic assessment.

## 7. Assessment System

Use a 100-point assessment rubric:

1. Aufgabenbewältigung: 20 points
2. Inhalt und Entwicklung: 15 points
3. Wortschatz: 20 points
4. Grammatik: 20 points
5. Kohärenz und Kohäsion: 15 points
6. Register und Stil: 5 points
7. Rechtschreibung und Zeichensetzung: 5 points

Grade system:

- 90–100: A
- 80–89: B
- 70–79: C
- 60–69: D
- 50–59: E
- 0–49: F

CEFR assessment must be based on CEFR descriptors, not a direct conversion from numerical scores.

Show individual skill levels and confidence.

## 8. AI Assessment

Implement four separate AI functions:

A. Original Writing Assessment\
B. Grammar and Vocabulary Correction\
C. Educational Feedback and Lessons\
D. Improved Writing Versions

AI must evaluate the original submission only.

Never calculate the original score from an AI-rewritten version.

Every error must include:

- Original text
- Corrected text
- Error category
- Error explanation in Thai
- Relevant German grammar rule
- Additional examples
- Severity
- Confidence
- Text position

Distinguish actual errors from optional stylistic improvements.

Avoid double penalization.

## 9. Improved Writing

Generate three separate versions:

1. Corrected Version
2. Improved B2 Version
3. Advanced C1 Model Version

Preserve the original meaning.

Clearly label the B2 and C1 versions as learning examples rather than the learner's actual writing level.

## 10. Learning Center

Include:

- German grammar lessons
- Vocabulary learning
- Collocation examples
- Connector lessons
- Error-based exercises
- Personalized recommendations

Prioritize repeated mistakes.

## 11. User Dashboard

Show:

- Total writing submissions
- Average writing score
- Estimated CEFR profile
- Score history
- Grammar weaknesses
- Vocabulary development
- Connector usage
- Learning recommendations

## 12. Database

Use Supabase PostgreSQL.

Implement:

- profiles
- user_preferences
- writing_tasks
- task_requirements
- writing_drafts
- writing_submissions
- assessments
- assessment_errors
- vocabulary_bank
- grammar_lessons
- learning_progress
- learning_recommendations
- rubric_versions
- assessment_audit_logs

Enable Row Level Security on all user-specific data.

Users must only access their own submissions, assessments, vocabulary, and learning history.

## 13. UI Design

Use a clean, minimal academic design.

Primary color: Navy Blue.\
Secondary color: Blue.\
Background: White / Light Gray.\
Typography: Inter.

Prioritize readability, accessibility, responsive layouts, and a professional educational appearance.

The writing editor and assessment results are the most important interfaces.

## 14. Assessment Reliability

- Validate every AI response using JSON Schema.
- Recalculate scores on the backend.
- Verify category score totals.
- Verify error positions against original text.
- Store AI model and rubric versions.
- Handle failed AI requests safely.
- Never fabricate grammar errors.
- Support assessment calibration and human review.

## 15. Development Requirements

Develop in stages:

Phase 1: Authentication, UI, Database.\
Phase 2: Writing Tasks and Editor.\
Phase 3: AI Assessment and Correction.\
Phase 4: Dashboard, History and Learning Center.

Build working functionality, not static mockups.

Use reusable components, clean TypeScript architecture, secure API endpoints, database migrations, and proper error handling.

Start by building the MVP with complete authentication, database integration, writing submission, assessment, and history functionality.

Before implementing advanced features, ensure that the complete submission-to-assessment workflow works correctly.

# 16. ข้อเสนอแนะก่อนเริ่มพัฒนาจริง

มี 3 เรื่องที่ผมอยากเน้นเป็นพิเศษ

1\. ความแม่นยำสำคัญกว่าความสวยของเว็บไซต์

อย่าเพิ่งสร้างระบบ AI ที่ซับซ้อนมากตั้งแต่วันแรก ควรสร้างชุดข้อสอบและคำตอบตัวอย่างที่ผู้เชี่ยวชาญตรวจแล้ว เพื่อใช้ทดสอบ AI ก่อน

2\. ต้องแยก Academic Assessment ออกจาก Learning Mode

- Academic Assessment: ตรวจเข้มงวด ประเมินงานต้นฉบับ ไม่มีคำใบ้ระหว่างเขียน
- Learning Mode: ให้คำอธิบาย ตัวอย่าง และแบบฝึกหัดอย่างเต็มที่

แม้จะใช้ระบบเดียวกัน แต่ต้องไม่ทำให้การช่วยสอนส่งผลต่อคะแนนสอบ

3\. CEFR ต้องเป็น Skill Profile ไม่ใช่แค่ตัวอักษรเดียว

ผู้เรียนอาจมี Grammar ระดับ B1 แต่ Vocabulary ระดับ B2 และ Content ระดับ C1 ได้ ระบบจึงควรแสดงภาพรวมทุกด้าน ไม่ใช่บอกเพียงว่าเป็น B2

